@meta
	company: ACME Corp
	amount: $1,000,000
@end

# Table Corpus Tests

This file exercises all table LDOC features.

## Basic Table

Simple table with header row (first row) and data rows:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Header 1
		@cell: Header 2
		@cell: Header 3
	@row
		@cell: Cell A1
		@cell: Cell A2
		@cell: Cell A3
	@row
		@cell: Cell B1
		@cell: Cell B2
		@cell: Cell B3
	@row
		@cell: Cell C1
		@cell: Cell C2
		@cell: Cell C3

## Horizontal Merge (Colspan)

Use colspan to merge cells horizontally:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Column A
		@cell: Column B
		@cell: Column C
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 2): Spans two columns
		@cell: Normal cell
	@row
		@cell: Normal
		@cell(colspan: 2): Spans two columns
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 3): All three columns span
	@row
		@cell: A
		@cell: B
		@cell: C

## Vertical Merge (Rowspan)

Use rowspan to merge cells vertically:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Header A
		@cell: Header B
		@cell: Header C
	@row
		@cell(rowspan: 3): Spans down
		@cell: Value 1
		@cell: Value 2
	@row
		@cell: Value 3
		@cell: Value 4
	@row
		@cell: Value 5
		@cell: Value 6
	@row
		@cell: Normal
		@cell: Normal
		@cell: Normal

## Combined Horizontal and Vertical Merge

Both colspan and rowspan in the same table:

@table
	@row
		@cell: A
		@cell: B
		@cell: C
		@cell: D
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 2, rowspan: 2): Spans 2x2
		@cell: Normal C
		@cell: Normal D
	@row
		@cell: More C
		@cell: More D
	@row
		@cell: Bottom A
		@cell: Bottom B
		@cell: Bottom C
		@cell: Bottom D

@table
	@row
		@cell: Col 1
		@cell: Col 2
		@cell: Col 3
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 2): Wide cell
		@cell(rowspan: 3): Tall cell
	@row
		@cell: Regular 1
		@cell: Regular 2
	@row
		@cell: Regular 3
		@cell: Regular 4

## Inline Formatting in Cells

Cells can contain **bold**, *italic*, and other inline formatting:

@table
	@row
		@cell: **Bold Header**
		@cell: *Italic Header*
		@cell: Normal Header
	@row
		@cell: **bold text**
		@cell: *italic text*
		@cell: normal text
	@row
		@cell: mixed **bold** and *italic*
		@cell: plain
		@cell: more plain
	@row
		@cell: `inline code`
		@cell: plain
		@cell: more plain

## Variables in Cells

Cells can contain variable references (defined at top of file):

@table
	@row
		@cell: Field
		@cell: Value
	@row
		@cell: Company Name
		@cell: {{company}}
	@row
		@cell: Contract Amount
		@cell: {{amount}}
	@row
		@cell: Description
		@cell: Payment to {{company}} for {{amount}}

## Quoting Cell Values

Special characters work directly in v2 syntax:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Header
		@cell: Special Values
	@row
		@cell: Comma in cell
		@cell: Hello, World
	@row
		@cell: Greater than literal
		@cell: >
	@row
		@cell: Caret literal
		@cell: ^
	@row
		@cell: Leading space
		@cell:  starts with space
	@row
		@cell: Trailing space
		@cell: ends with space 
	@row
		@cell: Quote marks
		@cell: He said "hello"

## Single Column Table

@table
	@row
		@cell: Single Column Header
	@row
		@cell: Row 1
	@row
		@cell: Row 2
	@row
		@cell: Row 3

## Single Row Table (Header Only)

@table
	@row
		@cell: Column A
		@cell: Column B
		@cell: Column C

## Empty Cells

@table
	@row
		@cell: Header A
		@cell: Header B
		@cell: Header C
	@row
		@cell:
		@cell: Value 2
		@cell: Value 3
	@row
		@cell: Value 1
		@cell:
		@cell: Value 3
	@row
		@cell: Value 1
		@cell: Value 2
		@cell:
	@row
		@cell:
		@cell:
		@cell:

## Complex Merge Pattern

@table
	@row
		@cell: A
		@cell: B
		@cell: C
		@cell: D
		@cell: E
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 3): Span 3 cols
		@cell: D1
		@cell: E1
	@row
		@cell: A2
		@cell: B2
		@cell: C2
		@cell(rowspan: 2): Span 2 rows
		@cell: E2
	@row
		@cell: A3
		@cell: B3
		@cell: C3
		@cell: E3
	@row
		@cell(colspan: 2, rowspan: 2): Span 2x2
		@cell: C4
		@cell: D4
		@cell: E4
	@row
		@cell: C5
		@cell: D5
		@cell: E5

## Table with @end Marker

@table
	@row
		@cell: With End
		@cell: Header 2
	@row
		@cell: Row 1
		@cell: Data 1
	@row
		@cell: Row 2
		@cell: Data 2
@end

Some text after the table.

## Multiple Tables in Sequence

First table:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Table 1 Col A
		@cell: Table 1 Col B
	@row
		@cell: T1 R1 A
		@cell: T1 R1 B

Second table:

@table
	@row
		@cell: Table 2 Col A
		@cell: Table 2 Col B
	@row
		@cell: T2 R1 A
		@cell: T2 R1 B

## Table with Links

@table
	@row
		@cell: Link Type
		@cell: Example
	@row
		@cell: Plain link
		@cell: [Click here](https://example.com)
	@row
		@cell: Bold link
		@cell: [**Bold link**](https://example.org)

## Long Cell Content

@table
	@row
		@cell: Short
		@cell: Long Content Column
	@row
		@cell: A
		@cell: This is a much longer piece of text that demonstrates how cells handle longer content strings
	@row
		@cell: B
		@cell: Another long cell with plenty of words to fill the space

End of table corpus tests.
